// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Diversity-through-preamble-seeding isocyanate SMILES CSD.
//
// Empirical baseline: Attempt 9 (T=1.6, 10 examples, N=C=O check) = 20% unique.
// Regressions: T=2.0 gave 10%, more examples gave 3-4%.
//
// Root-cause diagnosis:
//   All 100 runs share IDENTICAL prompt+generatedPrefix context before the
//   constrained span opens. With a fixed context and finite LM entropy, the
//   model revisits the same ~10-20 isocyanate templates repeatedly.
//
// Core NEW mechanism: 5-token unconstrained preamble BEFORE opening "<<".
//   Because the LM is sampled stochastically, each of the 100 independent
//   runs generates a DIFFERENT 5-token preamble. Those preamble tokens become
//   part of the stable prefix embedded in constrainedPrompt when we later
//   decode inside the span. A unique preamble context → unique LM distribution
//   → structurally different SMILES across runs.
//   This is purely a cross-run diversity mechanism; it does not alter the
//   parser-validity guarantees.
//
// Birthday-problem estimate:
//   Unique per-run seeding + T=1.6 → K_eff ≈ 50 effective unique paths
//   → E[unique in 100] ≈ 50*(1-e^{-2}) ≈ 43  (above 36% threshold).
//
// All constrained-phase parameters remain identical to attempt 9 (best result):
//   - Same 10-example guidance (N=C=O framing)
//   - N=C=O check forces continuation for O=C=N-format SMILES (dominant format),
//     producing longer, more varied molecules before closure
//   - T=1.6 for mid/late constrained generation
//   - SafePenalizedConstrainedStep for first 6 SMILES tokens (penalise "C","CC","O")
//   - GroupBoostedConstrainedStep for tokenCount >= 18
//   - minSpanLength = 5
//   - CloseSpanWithinBudget fallback
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Preamble loop: the guard requires !insideConstrainedOut on entry; the only
//     path that sets insideConstrainedOut := true also sets currentConstrainedOut := [],
//     which is valid by precondition. After that, the guard fails and the loop exits. ✓
//   OpenConstrainedSpan: sets currentConstrainedOut := []; valid by precondition. ✓
//   IsCompletePrefix + hasNCO>0 → CloseConstrainedSpan: sets insideConstrainedOut := false,
//     implication vacuous; currentConstrainedOut := []. ✓
//   IsCompletePrefix + hasNCO=0 → SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep: hard-masks to
//     parser-valid tokens ∪ EOS; AppendConstrainedToken preserves IsValidPrefix. ✓
//   IsCompletePrefix + hasNCO=0 + EOS → CloseConstrainedSpan: same as close case. ✓
//   Else (not complete): SafePenalized / SafeTemperature / GroupBoosted all
//     hard-mask to parser-valid ∪ EOS; AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity. ✓
//   EOS in else + close: CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false;
//     implication vacuous. ✓
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget: postcondition guarantees insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut). ✓
//
// Invariant 2 (progress): |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Preamble loop: UnconstrainedStep costs 1 step; EOS: step up, no append,
//     balance maintained; token: step up, generated grows by 1, exactly balanced. ✓
//   OpenConstrainedSpan: costs 1 step, appends "<<" (1 token); balanced. ✓
//   IsCompletePrefix + hasNCO>0 → Close: costs 1 step, appends ">>" (1 token); balanced. ✓
//   IsCompletePrefix + hasNCO=0 → SafeTemperature (1 step) then either append
//     (≤1 token) or EOS + Close (1 more step + 1 token ">>"); net ≤+2 steps for ≤+1
//     visible tokens in the temp branch, then +1 for close, total ≤+2 steps ≤ steps
//     growth. Invariant preserved. ✓
//   Else: 1 step, ≤1 token (non-EOS) or EOS+close (+2 steps, +1 token ">>"); ✓
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget: closeBudget = maxSteps - steps;
//     |generatedOut| <= |generated| + closeBudget <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps;
//     steps := maxSteps. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
